Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.30,0:00:13.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, you're saying you can't tell us, no matter what?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.72,0:00:20.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You see, there's this alien—
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.68,0:00:20.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Scieszka, keep quiet.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.31,0:00:23.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Still, you couldn't have wound up in the power distribution station
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.48,0:00:25.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,just because you'd\Nlost your way, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.31,0:00:27.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What exactly were you\Ndoing in there?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.31,0:00:28.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sergeant...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.48,0:00:32.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you\Ngoing to do now?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.20,0:00:44.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, Lieutenant Ross...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.29,0:00:49.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's something going on\Nwithin the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.04,0:00:51.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Something very dangerous.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.42,0:00:55.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.18,0:01:03.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Winry-san, \Nwhat do we do now?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.18,0:01:05.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going back to\NResembool for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.56,0:01:11.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'd like to talk to Ed and Al, \Nbut I don't know where they are.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.19,0:01:11.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then what should I do?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.44,0:01:14.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.19,0:01:16.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're coming with me!\NBut what about\Nmy books at home?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.82,0:01:17.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Leave them there.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.84,0:01:42.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.55,0:01:44.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can take this off now, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.02,0:01:47.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Be my guest.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.90,0:01:52.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ah, that's better.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.36,0:01:54.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Crimson...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.53,0:01:59.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, well, if it isn't the Flame Major—make that Colonel.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.24,0:02:01.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is something the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.28,0:02:03.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Archer!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.41,0:02:05.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is the meaning of this?!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.04,0:02:10.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you have some issue with the Crimson Alchemist, Lt. Colonel Zolf J. Kimbly?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.79,0:02:11.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Colonel?!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.63,0:02:16.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Lt. Colonel was imprisoned on false charges,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.76,0:02:21.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and just before he was subjected to unlawful human experimentation at the 5th Laboratory,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.30,0:02:23.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,he made a successful escape.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.10,0:02:25.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thanks to the Lt.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.72,0:02:28.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel's testimony, the facts about the 5th Laboratory are coming to light.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.89,0:02:31.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,False charges?!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.14,0:02:32.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's outrageous!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.90,0:02:36.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do not forget that \Nfor this operation,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.03,0:02:40.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the Führer has granted me\Nthe rank of colonel.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.66,0:02:46.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By the way, who was\Nthat telephone call from?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.79,0:02:47.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.04,0:02:50.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you know of\Na town called Liore?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.13,0:03:00.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.94,0:03:15.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Man cannot obtain anything\Nwithout first sacrificing something.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.65,0:03:20.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to obtain anything,\Nsomething of equal value is required.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.90,0:03:25.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is alchemy's\NLaw of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.66,0:03:31.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the time, we believed that\Nto be the true way of the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.73,0:05:19.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, you're the one...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.36,0:05:22.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.36,0:05:23.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I killed Greed.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.36,0:05:25.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.44,0:05:27.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What good\Ndoes it do to say that now?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.20,0:05:30.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Martel, I don't know \Nwhat you were thinking,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.70,0:05:34.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but to me, you and Greed were both criminals who kidnapped my brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.58,0:05:38.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's more,\Nhe also killed Dante-san.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.71,0:05:42.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Martel-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.76,0:05:48.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Look out!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.30,0:05:54.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A snake?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.89,0:06:00.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're not who I'm after.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.48,0:06:05.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Greed-san chose death\Nrather than being sealed up again.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.65,0:06:08.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He was, more than anything,\Na proud man.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.40,0:06:12.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And so, I believe he wanted to be defeated by you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.87,0:06:20.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The ones who I detest are \Nthe military who killed my friends,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.74,0:06:20.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and those two\Nwho dress all in black,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.83,0:06:23.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,as well as the man\Nwho betrayed my friends.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.17,0:06:25.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Kimbly!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.35,0:06:34.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why don't you eat it?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.51,0:06:36.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They're nutritious.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.68,0:06:39.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why don't {\i1}you{\i0} eat it?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.56,0:06:40.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, my.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.48,0:06:43.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If I did that, it would be cannibalism, wouldn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.99,0:06:53.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're getting close to Liore, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.57,0:06:55.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.20,0:06:58.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wonder how Rose-san is doing.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.79,0:07:00.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.58,0:07:02.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't pretend you've forgotten.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.42,0:07:04.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, you've been a little worried about her, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.42,0:07:07.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, Martel, how soon\Nbefore we get to Ishbal?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.09,0:07:08.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're here.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.05,0:07:11.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've long since entered Ishbal.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.85,0:07:24.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is Ishbal?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.19,0:07:27.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's nothing here,\Nhuh, Brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.57,0:07:31.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We need some way\Nto find Scar, but this...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.40,0:07:33.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What exactly are you\Nlooking for, anyway?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.83,0:07:40.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.58,0:07:42.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There was a man who said
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.50,0:07:45.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,they had created a Philosopher's Stone before Ishbal was destroyed.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.71,0:07:48.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That can't be true.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.46,0:07:52.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They offered no resistance\Nand were killed before they\Nhad a chance to take up arms.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.92,0:07:54.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No way they offered\Nno resistance!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.22,0:07:59.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The military and Ishbal had\Na long and tense military relationship.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.35,0:08:02.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then an incident where a soldier mistakenly shot a civilian took place,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.19,0:08:05.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and the Ishbalans rose up.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.35,0:08:09.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So that's really\Nhow it was presented...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.57,0:08:12.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I didn't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.78,0:08:15.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I was in that laboratory for a little over fourteen years.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.24,0:08:19.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Since just after the civil war in Ishbal broke out?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.83,0:08:22.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thanks to being turned into a Chimera,\NI may look young,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.20,0:08:23.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but I'm your fairly older sister.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.08,0:08:24.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean aunt—
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.25,0:08:27.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.84,0:08:33.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We were a special operations unit.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.19,0:08:47.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We weren't told\Nwhat our destination was
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.56,0:08:52.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,or what the details of our mission were\Nuntil the last minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.49,0:08:55.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's the way\Nthey usually did it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.87,0:09:00.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's going on?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.71,0:09:11.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're in dire straits!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.88,0:09:12.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}What's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.76,0:09:16.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}I don't know! But people are being killed!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.76,0:09:17.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The mission we had been given \Nwas to infiltrate the Ishbalan city
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.01,0:09:19.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and conduct large-scale subversive activities.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.01,0:09:19.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}In any case, let's get someplace safe!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.22,0:09:23.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was under the pretext of preventing them\Nfrom carrying out acts of terrorism
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.77,0:09:26.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that they were planning to commit against Central.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.04,0:09:53.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And you're saying that's what\Nbrought about the Ishbalan uprising?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.42,0:09:56.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What reason would the military have for starting a war with Ishbal?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.01,0:09:58.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't know\Nwhat the reason was.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.47,0:09:59.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There, you see?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.68,0:10:01.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But I do have proof.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.98,0:10:11.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't get it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.23,0:10:14.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just listen to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.82,0:10:21.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right after the Ishbalan\NCivil War started,\Nwe were placed in custody.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.57,0:10:24.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Anyone who resisted...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.66,0:10:25.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dammit!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.91,0:10:28.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's going on here?!\NWe were following military orders!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.26,0:10:43.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those who survived were\Ntaken to the 5th Laboratory.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.14,0:10:51.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dolcetto!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.27,0:10:53.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Martel!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.28,0:11:02.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.57,0:11:04.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Martel!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.47,0:11:26.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They made you a Chimera.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.93,0:11:30.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The military tried to\Ncompletely silence us.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.48,0:11:31.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.89,0:11:34.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Because you knew a secret that\Nabsolutely could not be leaked out—
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.94,0:11:36.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the truth about\Nthe start of the war.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.94,0:11:38.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But why?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.44,0:11:40.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why would the military\Nprovoke Ishbal?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.05,0:11:45.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Someone's there?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.05,0:11:45.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.45,0:11:46.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a lead!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.83,0:11:49.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're not getting away!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.63,0:12:05.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Now then, let's have you tell me \Nwhat you're doing here.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.30,0:12:09.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Th-This area is\Noff-limits to civilians.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.35,0:12:13.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're here to check on the security of the old Ishbalan cities.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.60,0:12:17.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then you could've just shown yourselves instead of sneaking around, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.48,0:12:22.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah. He may not look it, \Nbut my brother is a State Alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.95,0:12:26.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you guys, moles?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.62,0:12:30.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, could those men be...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.84,0:12:39.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yo...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.00,0:12:41.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You guys...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.13,0:12:43.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then the Colonel is here too?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.23,0:13:00.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well aren't you a familiar face?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.94,0:13:05.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, yeah, same old shrimp who's so small
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.78,0:13:05.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,you'd lose sight of him\Namong the grains of san—
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.86,0:13:06.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who are you calling that?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.12,0:13:12.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I hear you've been raising hell\Nall over the place.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.37,0:13:16.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Southern Command Center,\Nas well as the Ishbalan escort train.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.63,0:13:23.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Anyhow, you're under\Nmy command from now on.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.17,0:13:25.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just a moment, please!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.26,0:13:28.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're lucky that Havoc caught you when they were out scouting.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.47,0:13:32.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But we're supposed to have permission to continue our journey independently.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.18,0:13:37.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, once called up,\NI become a dog of the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.44,0:13:38.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.94,0:13:43.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They've come all the way out to this\Nremote region in a military transport train.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.57,0:13:49.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't tell me there's a war.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.07,0:13:53.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're just quelling\Na somewhat seditious area.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.33,0:13:57.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Our target is a town about two\Nkilometers south-southeast of here.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.33,0:13:59.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're pretty heavily armed, considering.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.67,0:14:00.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are we?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.58,0:14:03.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Shall I tell you why you're here?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.46,0:14:04.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's Scar, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.26,0:14:09.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We were just looking\Nfor him ourselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.39,0:14:16.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are your reasons\Nfor pursuing Scar?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.02,0:14:21.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we don't put him down,\Nhe's going to make a lot of trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.40,0:14:24.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, Alphonse-kun,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.23,0:14:27.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,you don't have to force yourself to pretend you're eating.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.53,0:14:29.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Y-Yes, you're right.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.61,0:14:32.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll kill that woman!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.79,0:14:37.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.91,0:14:41.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The latest photographs\Nfrom our surveillance balloon.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.38,0:14:48.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.92,0:14:50.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It couldn't be...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.34,0:14:53.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A transmutation circle\Nmade from the whole city?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.42,0:15:07.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who would do such a thing?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.48,0:15:07.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I won!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.28,0:15:08.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Scar.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.44,0:15:09.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So it {\i1}is{\i0} him?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.45,0:15:13.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Edward-kun, do you know what his objective is?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.03,0:15:15.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.28,0:15:18.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, what town is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.29,0:15:19.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The town is named Liore.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.91,0:15:24.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Last year, its tyrannical priest retired,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.38,0:15:26.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and peace has just barely returned with the stationing of troops there.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.85,0:15:28.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sergeant Fuery...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.98,0:15:28.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sir?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.63,0:15:30.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He knows.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.30,0:15:33.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Liore, you say?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.39,0:15:36.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,An armed uprising in Liore?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.97,0:15:38.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This shouldn't be happening!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.64,0:15:40.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We put down that bogus priest and brought peace to the city!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.02,0:15:41.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.64,0:15:46.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After that, the people divided into\Na priest faction and a citizen's faction,\Nand there has been\Nterrible confusion.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.02,0:15:51.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When the military went in\Nto gather a situation report,\Nboth factions stood against them.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.53,0:15:54.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why didn't you\Ntell me about this?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.66,0:15:56.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I was involved in this\Nfrom the start!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.28,0:15:59.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I heard the report from Hughes, but I kept it back.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.58,0:16:00.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.50,0:16:02.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Because it was too much for you to handle.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.18,0:16:18.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't Ed-kun and Al-kun know about Brigadier General Hughes?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.55,0:16:20.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Apparently not.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.31,0:16:24.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If he tells them now, they'd probably just dash back to Central, and all.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.56,0:16:27.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He is an important military asset,\Nand everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.02,0:16:32.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Edward-kun and his brother are in a dangerous position right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.94,0:16:38.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He probably wants to have them in a place where he can keep his eye on them.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.83,0:16:45.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, is my brother here?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.54,0:16:51.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You will give me first priority when reporting.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.13,0:16:56.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And if you will observe my earlier conditions, \NI will grant you permission.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.68,0:16:59.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed! What are you doing here?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.31,0:17:03.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At his insistence,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.14,0:17:06.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am having him\Nreconnoiter the town of Liore.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.77,0:17:10.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're sending one of our precious State Alchemists out to sightsee?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.65,0:17:14.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Which is exactly why no matter what happens,\Nhe will come back to us alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.15,0:17:15.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Besides,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.74,0:17:18.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,he knows more about Liore than anyone else does.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.49,0:17:21.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please put your mind at ease.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.45,0:17:25.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He said he would\Nleave his brother here.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.25,0:17:31.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's not about to leave his dear brother here and disappear by himself on us, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.88,0:17:35.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why didn't you tell me?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.01,0:17:37.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If I had, would you have given me permission?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.72,0:17:40.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've learned about Liore, and now you're confused.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.51,0:17:46.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's why I'm going to\Ncool my head now.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.15,0:17:56.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Phew, it was hot in there.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.61,0:17:57.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Be careful.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.99,0:18:00.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The way the military sees it, you're a wanted person.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.28,0:18:04.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, are you serious about this? You're going to Liore alone?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.37,0:18:09.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Leaving you behind\Nwas the bargaining point.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.08,0:18:13.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Archer doesn't trust us at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.38,0:18:17.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wonder if that transmutation circle is for a Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.59,0:18:19.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If it is, I'm going to destroy it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.34,0:18:22.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Martel, behave yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.22,0:18:28.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know. I held myself back in front of \Nthat Archer guy earlier, didn't I?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.43,0:18:31.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to kill those guys in black and Kimbly first.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.56,0:18:34.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Taking my revenge against\Nthe military comes after that.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.11,0:18:36.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm not going to let you\Ndo that, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.28,0:18:45.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, be really careful, okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.79,0:18:46.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.17,0:18:53.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,M-Major...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.59,0:18:55.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're here?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.55,0:19:00.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel Archer said to\Nleave your silver watch here.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.76,0:19:02.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.14,0:19:05.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I guess it would be trouble if someone found out my position.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.85,0:19:15.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Edward Elric,\Nwhy did you come here?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.94,0:19:19.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fate, maybe?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.53,0:19:20.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's not like you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.28,0:19:24.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I doubt you two\Neven believe in fate.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.17,0:19:38.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A new silver watch has arrived.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.84,0:19:45.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Give this one the transmutation amplification treatment as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.95,0:20:11.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that right?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.12,0:20:15.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You were driven out of the city because of that priest, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.54,0:20:19.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That Cornello guy was\Npositively awful, all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.63,0:20:24.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By the way, I get the feeling that \NI've seen your face around somewhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.22,0:20:26.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.51,0:20:28.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Must be one of those\Ncommon faces.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.31,0:20:32.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's the Holy Mother!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.77,0:20:37.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're in luck!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.15,0:20:37.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.69,0:20:40.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's the Holy Mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.54,0:21:01.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Rose?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.92,0:21:06.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please go back inside!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.13,0:21:09.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Colonel said that under no circumstances was anyone to see you!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.01,0:21:12.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Because I'm officially deceased?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.22,0:21:14.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At least allow me to do as I like\Nin the evening.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.10,0:21:16.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.27,0:21:17.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You sure are pesky.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:23.86,0:21:24.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.36,0:21:28.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Kimbly!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.32,0:21:30.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey there.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.87,0:21:37.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,To think that we would be\Nseeing the boy here again...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.87,0:21:41.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What should we do, Gluttony?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.88,0:21:45.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Pride told us, right?\NThe Ishbal...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.22,0:21:47.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,um...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.01,0:21:51.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Kill anyone who knows the truth about Ishbal.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.64,0:21:52.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's too bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.27,0:21:57.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I smell it. I smell it!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.35,0:22:02.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The smell of the Ishbalan beast!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.41,0:23:40.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.08,0:23:42.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 40: "The Scar"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.96,0:23:47.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Some people say that the scars\Non your body disappear in time.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.46,0:23:51.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But there are some scars that you can't get rid of.
